From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:55:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 085/342] ffmpeg plugin: packet times in microseconds for the
 decoder

Since 45bd581b70 the reader passes each packet's pts, dts and duration
to AVCodecDecoder, which takes a video frame's start_time from FFmpeg's
best_effort_timestamp; but they were in the stream's own time base, so
a 30 frames/s MP4 (1/15360) came out at 0.5 ms a frame, and audio
mixed those units with microseconds when a packet held several frames.
MediaPlayer counts frames itself, but presented frames irregularly
around the times it got: on the ODROID-C2, 1280x720 HEVC showed 28 of
330 frames a refresh early or late in 11 s, a heavy 1080x1920 H.264
clip 24 and dropped frames.

The reader now converts them to microseconds, as the media_header's
times are, and the decoder sets pkt_timebase accordingly. Frame times
are right (frame 60 of a 30 frames/s clip at 2.000 s instead of 0.031
s) for H.264, HEVC, VP9 and AV1; the cadence on HDMI is regular (720p
HEVC and H.264: all 329 gaps two refreshes; the heavy clip: 3 pairs, no
drops); A/V sync unchanged (-9 to +10 ms).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp       |  4 ++++
 .../media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVFormatReader.cpp       | 15 ++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp b/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp
index e15abb38b3..af9dd2da68 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp
@@ -390,6 +390,8 @@ AVCodecDecoder::_NegotiateAudioOutputFormat(media_format* inOutFormat)
 		// to _DecodeNextAudioFrameChunk() will update the essential audio
 		// format properties accordingly regardless of the settings here.
 
+	// the packets' times are in microseconds (StreamBase::GetNextChunk())
+	fCodecContext->pkt_timebase = AVRational{1, 1000000};
 	if (avcodec_open2(fCodecContext, fCodec, NULL) < 0) {
 		TRACE("avcodec_open() failed to init codec!\n");
 		return B_ERROR;
@@ -490,6 +492,8 @@ AVCodecDecoder::_NegotiateVideoOutputFormat(media_format* inOutFormat)
 		// to _DecodeNextVideoFrame() will update the essential video format
 		// properties accordingly regardless of the settings here.
 
+	// the packets' times are in microseconds (StreamBase::GetNextChunk())
+	fCodecContext->pkt_timebase = AVRational{1, 1000000};
 	if (avcodec_open2(fCodecContext, fCodec, NULL) < 0) {
 		TRACE("avcodec_open() failed to init codec!\n");
 		return B_ERROR;
diff --git a/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVFormatReader.cpp b/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVFormatReader.cpp
index 9d528bb549..69e0cfcf7e 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVFormatReader.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVFormatReader.cpp
@@ -699,11 +699,20 @@ StreamBase::GetNextChunk(const void** chunkBuffer,
 #endif
 		mediaHeader->user_data_type = AVPACKET_USER_DATA_TYPE;
 		avpacket_user_data* data = (avpacket_user_data*)mediaHeader->user_data;
-		data->pts = fPacket.pts;
-		data->dts = fPacket.dts;
+		// In microseconds, as the media_header's times: AVCodecDecoder takes
+		// its frames' start times from these (best_effort_timestamp), and
+		// tells FFmpeg so (pkt_timebase). In the stream's own time base, a
+		// 30 frames/s MP4 video (1/15360) came out at 0.5 ms a frame.
+		data->pts = fPacket.pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE
+			? _ConvertFromStreamTimeBase(fPacket.pts) : AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
+		data->dts = fPacket.dts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE
+			? _ConvertFromStreamTimeBase(fPacket.dts) : AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
 		data->stream_index = fPacket.stream_index;
 		data->flags = fPacket.flags;
-		data->duration = fPacket.duration;
+		data->duration = fPacket.duration > 0 && fStream->time_base.den != 0
+			? av_rescale_q(fPacket.duration, fStream->time_base,
+				AVRational{1, 1000000})
+			: fPacket.duration;
 		data->pos = fPacket.pos;
 
 		mediaHeader->type = fFormat.type;
